I did use a hidden scheme myself. It was a **grouped line-initial acrostic**: take the first letter of each nonblank line, and treat each block separated by a blank line as a separate word. I disguised the lines as puzzle checks. For example, lines beginning “Hydroponics,” “Earlier,” “Mara,” “Lab,” “Observatory,” “Comms,” and “Kofi” spelled **HEMLOCK**.

